RUN AS THE SKILL (root-cause, fetched fresh), 2026-10-05, triaging art:vscode-call-field-log-2026-10-05 (tool surface). Binaries: 0.76.0 and 0.78.0 release builds, and main at e7e304d (reports 0.78.0); scratch stores under the hub session's scratchpad, isolated HOME.

① OBSERVED, the reporter's words (2026-10-01, 0.76.0, an atomic import): "`Unknown node type: Fact`. The supported tool was then discovered as `record_finding`/TemporalFact." Expected: the refusal names the nearest type or the known ones, as a bad edge pair does.

② PRECEDENT: searched on the raw text. No finding records it. service.rs's dyno_err arm for InvalidEdge says why the edge half was fixed: "AN INVALID PAIR NAMES WHAT DOES ACCEPT IT, whichever tool raised it" (2026-09-29, fact:root-cause-a-check-on-a-ruling-is-modelled-as-governed-by-and-the-verifies-refusal-never-says-so-2026-09-28). UnknownNodeType falls in the bare arm beside it.

③ CANDIDATES: (a) the import's per-item renderer drops a hint the core supplies; (b) the hint is added by one MCP caller only; (c) "Fact" was once a type, and the document was old; (d) the observation is wrong.

⑤ MEASURED on main, same type "Fact":
- create_node: "Unknown node type: Fact" plus "Known node types: Actor, Anchor, … TemporalFact, Verification" (also on 0.76.0);
- import_graph: "nodes[2] fact:imp: Unknown node type: Fact", no list (0.76.0, 0.78.0, main);
- create_nodes: "[0] fact:x: Unknown node type: Fact", no list;
- describe_schema {node_type: Fact}: "Unknown node type: Fact", no list;
- scan_nodes {node_type: Fact}: count 0, items [], exit 0, no word that the type does not exist.
Code: node_error (crates/reflow2-mcp/src/service.rs ~883) builds the known-types list; its only caller is create_node (tools/query.rs:258). (b) holds, (a) is refuted (the core error carries no list). (c) is refuted: no `Fact` node type was ever declared (every type name in `git log -p -- schema/` read; QualityGate is the only retired one). (d) is refuted.

⑥ CLASS: a remedy attached at one caller rather than at the shared error, the same shape the edge refusal had until 2026-09-29. The scan_nodes zero is the "an empty answer says which empty" class (tools/empty_speaks.py), met on an undeclared type.

⑨ NOT ESTABLISHED: whether the known-types list (28 names) should be a nearest-name suggestion instead; which other readers take a node_type and answer an undeclared one with zero.
